      "markdown": "3. (Singapore) $ ^{4} $ Let f be a polynomial of degree n, such that f(k) = \\frac{k}{k+1} for every integer 0 \\leq k \\leq n. Compute f(n+1).\n\n4. (USA) $ ^{5} $ Let f be a real polynomial of degree n, such that f(k) = \\binom{n+1}{k}^{-1} for 0 \\leq k \\leq n. Compute all possible values of f(n+1).\n\n5. (IMO—shortlist) A polynomial $f$, of degree 990, is such that $f(k) = F_k$ for $992 \\leq k \\leq 1982$, where $F_k$ stands for the $k$-th Fibonacci number. Prove that $f(1983) = F_{1983} - 1$.\n\n6. (IMO—shortlist) Let f be a real polynomial such that\n\n(a)  $ f(1) > f(0) > 0. $\n\n(b)  $ f(2) > 2f(1) - f(0). $\n\n(c)  $  f(3) > 3f(2) - 3f(1) + f(0).  $\n\n(d)  $  f(n + 4) > 4f(n + 3) - 6f(n + 2) + 4f(n + 1) - f(n)  $ for every  $ n \\in \\mathbb{N} $.\n\nProve that  $ f(n) > 0 $ for every  $ n \\in \\mathbb{N} $.",
